                      "t": "text",
                      "v": "My people, let it be known to you, I take no pleasure at all in what I must do, in what must be done - NO PLEASURE AT ALL! Says The Lord. As My hand draws back, blood pours down! As I strike the earth in My anger, My tears run down! As famine spreads forth across the land, My heart is rent inside Me over the hardness of men’s hearts! As My face fills with the heat of My fury, My eyes are set ablaze with fire over that which I see! My tears run down, My tears run down. As My own servants turn from Me and run, as My own beloved, whom I have called sons and daughters, turn and fight against Me, My body betrays Me,"
