            "ot": {
              "label": "Old Testament Prophecy",
              "sublabel": "As Moses Lifted Up the Serpent in the Wilderness, So Also Must The Messiah Be Lifted Up",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "para",
                  "segments": [
                    {
                      "t": "text",
                      "v": "So Moses made a bronze serpent, and put it on a pole; and so it was, if a serpent had bitten anyone, when he looked at the bronze serpent, he lived. - Numbers 21:9"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "para",
                  "segments": [
                    {
                      "t": "italic",
                      "v": "Though this verse was literally performed by the Israelites according to God's command through Moses, it was a foreshadowing of the crucifixion and its purpose... \"That through death The Messiah might destroy him who had the power of death, that is, the devil\" (Hebrews 2:14)."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "nt": {
              "label": "Fulfilled in the New Testament",
              "sublabel": "YahuShua Was Lifted Up On the Cross, So That Many Would Be Saved",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "para",
                  "segments": [
                    {
                      "t": "text",
                      "v": "And as Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, even so must The Son of Man be lifted up, that whoever believes in Him should not perish but have eternal life. For God so loved the world that He gave His only begotten Son, that whoever believes in Him should not perish but have everlasting life. For God did not send His Son into the world to condemn the world, but that the world through Him might be saved."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "para",
                  "segments": [
                    {
                      "t": "text",
                      "v": "He who believes in Him is not condemned; but he who does not believe is condemned already, because he has not believed in the name of The Only Begotten Son of God. - John 3:14-18"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
